{"name":"Red Gooseberry","hex":"#604046","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"gooseberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit of species Ribes uva-crispa, related to the currant.","Any other plant or fruit in the subgenus Grossularia, distinguished from currants by bearing spines, including Ribes hirtellum (American gooseberry)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gooseberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gooseberry","blocks":[{"text":"Gooseberry is a common name for many species of Ribes, as well as a large number of plants of similar appearance, and also several unrelated plants. The term gooseberry has a debated etymology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Stachelbeeren.jpg/330px-Stachelbeeren.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gooseberry"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Stachelbeere_%28Ribes_uva-crispa%29.jpg/500px-Stachelbeere_%28Ribes_uva-crispa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Stachelbeere_%28Ribes_uva-crispa%29.jpg/500px-Stachelbeere_%28Ribes_uva-crispa%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Red berries of Ribes uva-crispa ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStachelbeere_(Ribes_uva-crispa).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg/1280px-Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg/500px-Illustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ribes uva-crispa by Otto Wilhelm Thomé (1885), showing the distinctive curl of the flower petals[5]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustration_Ribes_uva-crispa0.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/Gooseberry_flower1.jpg/500px-Gooseberry_flower1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/dc/Gooseberry_flower1.jpg/500px-Gooseberry_flower1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conten